    "result_text": "The full suite is these acceptance tests, and both pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\nHere's what I implemented to satisfy the specification:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Request contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)**\n- Added optional structured fields `addressLine1` (non-blank, normalized) and `addressLine2` (optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list (it stays accepted for backward compatibility) while keeping `city` required, so earlier minimal owners still validate.\n- Registered a second class-level constraint `@AddressPresenceValidation` alongside the existing `@PostcodeValidation`. Since `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` live on `OwnerFields`, they're automatically returned on the `Owner` response too.\n\n**New validation (`rest/validation/`)**\n- `AddressPresenceValidation` + `AddressPresenceValidator`: an owner is valid only when it supplies a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a non-blank flat `address` (plus the already-required `city`).\n\n**Model (`model/Owner.java`)**\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with getters/setters and `toString` entries.\n\n**Mapping (`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`)**\n- Normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` on create, and composes the stored/returned `address` via a new `composeAddress`: normalized `addressLine1` with a single space + normalized `addressLine2` appended when present; otherwise it falls back to the normalized flat `address`.\n\n**Update path (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)**\n- The update endpoint now sets the structured fields and composed address consistently.\n\n**Schema SQL** \u2014 added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to the owners table in all four dialect scripts (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres), since the test profile runs with `ddl-auto=none`.\n\nThe household hash (last name + postcode), postcode validation (city + postcode), and locality (postcode-derived) all read `city`/`postcode`, which are shared across both address forms, so they naturally use the structured fields when present and remain correct for flat-only owners.\n\nNote: this is not a git repository, so I did not create any commit \u2014 let me know if you'd like me to initialize one.",
