    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive extension that follows the existing conventions of this codebase:\n\n- **Mapper helper placement is right.** `composeAddress` lives on `OwnerMapper` beside `normalizeAddress`, `normalizeTelephone`, `formatInitials`, etc. \u2014 the established home for `default` mapping/normalization helpers. The `toOwner` create path drives it through MapStruct (`expression`/`qualifiedByName`), matching the surrounding `@Mapping` style.\n\n- **Reuse, not duplication.** The single `composeAddress`/`normalizeAddress` logic is shared by both the create path (via MapStruct) and the `updateOwner` path (via direct calls). `updateOwner` already assigns fields individually with `setTelephone(normalizeTelephone(...))` / `setEmail(normalizeEmail(...))`; the new `setAddressLine1(normalizeAddress(...))` / `setAddressLine2(...)` / `setAddress(composeAddress(...))` lines extend that exact per-field pattern rather than inventing a new one.\n\n- **Validation follows house style.** `AddressPresenceValidation`/`AddressPresenceValidator` mirror the existing `PostcodeValidation`/`PostcodeValidator` pair precisely \u2014 class-level constraint over `OwnerFieldsDto`, null \u2192 true, wired via `x-class-extra-annotation` alongside the existing `PostcodeValidation`. A class-level constraint is the correct unit for a cross-field \"either/or\" check.\n\n- **Parallel, consistent peripheral changes.** The `Owner` entity gains matching getters/setters and `toString` entries; all four `schema.sql` dialects get the two nullable columns; the OpenAPI schema documents both new fields and relaxes the `address` requirement coherently.\n\nNo logic is misplaced, nothing is becoming a catch-all, and a maintainer of this repo would find each piece where they'd expect it.",
